.TH "PB-CONFIG-CONFLICT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-conflict - Inspect and resolve configuration conflicts


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config conflict [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect and resolve configuration conflicts

.PP
List current path conflicts, inspect one with show, then resolve it by choosing the machine or repository version. Resolution is explicit per path rather than a blanket overwrite.

.PP
Configuration commands distinguish local CLI settings from synchronized repository content. Inspect current state before changing it; synchronization reports conflicts instead of silently overwriting one side. The --json option provides structured output for scripts where supported.

.PP
With --json, this command group lists its available commands.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for conflict


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-conflict-list(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-conflict-resolve(1)\fP, \fBpb-config-conflict-show(1)\fP
